---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
---
<GuideLayout 
  title="Seamless vs. Cut & Sew: A Product Manager's Guide to Selection"
  type="CONSTRUCTION"
  date="July 03, 2026"
  readTime="7 min read"
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none font-['Century_Gothic',sans-serif] text-slate-800">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">The Technical Divide</h2>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
        Choosing the right manufacturing technology is the most critical decision a Product Manager makes during the development phase. While "Seamless" is often associated with high-end yoga wear, "Cut & Sew" remains the king of compression and shaping.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-8 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Seamless Technology</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4 italic">Best for: Yoga, pilates, and second-skin loungewear.</p>
          <ul class="list-none p-0 space-y-2 text-slate-700">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-green-600">✔</span> Zero irritation (no side seams)</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-green-600">✔</span> Engineered ventilation zones</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-green-600">✔</span> High elasticity and 3D fit</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-red-600"><span class="font-bold">✘</span> Limited compression support</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-red-600"><span class="font-bold">✘</span> Higher MOQs due to yarn dyeing</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-8 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Cut & Sew Technology</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4 italic">Best for: High-impact training, running, and shaping.</p>
          <ul class="list-none p-0 space-y-2 text-slate-700">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-green-600">✔</span> Maximum compression and support</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-green-600">✔</span> Unlimited design/pattern options</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-green-600">✔</span> Superior opaque (squat-proof) quality</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-red-600"><span class="font-bold">✘</span> Visible seams (Flatlock recommended)</li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-red-600"><span class="font-bold">✘</span> Higher waste during cutting phase</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">Decision Framework: Which to Choose?</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-6">
        As a Product Manager, you should base your decision on your **Target User Activity** and **Brand Aesthetic**:
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="border-l-4 border-gold pl-6 py-2">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900">Use Seamless IF:</h4>
          <p class="text-slate-600">Your brand values "softness" and a "lifestyle-fitness" crossover. It's ideal for customers who prioritize comfort over performance.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-l-4 border-slate-900 pl-6 py-2">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900">Use Cut & Sew IF:</h4>
          <p class="text-slate-600">Your brand is focused on "Hard Training" or "Body Sculpting." If you need to include mesh inserts, pockets, or complex color-blocking, Cut & Sew is the only option.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="bg-slate-900 text-white p-8 rounded-2xl mt-12">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Consult with Our Technical Designers</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-300 mb-6">Not sure which construction fits your next collection? Our tech team can provide a side-by-side comparison for your specific designs.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href="#inquiry" class="bg-[#C9A84C] text-black px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-bold hover:bg-[#b8973d] transition-colors">Book a Tech Review</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</GuideLayout>